            <fr:title text="FRI">FRI</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    Fast Reed–Solomon Interactive Oracle Proof of Proximity. The protocol most of the deployed proving stack rests on, and the one every construction later in this section is a response to.
</html:p>
            <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The folding map: halving the degree by splitting into even and odd parts and taking a random combination. Why the folded word is a codeword when the original is.</html:li>
        <html:li>Commit phase and query phase; the round-consistency check the verifier performs.</html:li>
        <html:li>Parameters and their interaction: rate, folding factor, number of rounds, number of query repetitions.</html:li>
        <html:li>Prover cost — encoding, Merkle hashing, and where the time actually goes.</html:li>
        <html:li><fr:link href="/dhsorens-004L/" title="Round-by-Round Soundness" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-004L/" display-uri="dhsorens-004L" type="local">The soundness statement</fr:link>, with the <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0038/" title="Soundness Regimes and the Proximity-Gap Conjectures" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0038/" display-uri="dhsorens-0038" type="local">regime</fr:link> named explicitly.</html:li>
        <html:li>What ArkLib's <html:code>ProofSystem/Fri</html:code> states, and how far the proof gets.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
            <html:p>
    Reading: Ben-Sasson, Bentov, Horesh, and Riabzev, <html:em>Fast Reed–Solomon Interactive Oracle Proofs of Proximity</html:em> (ICALP 2018); <fr:link href="https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/1367" type="external">the SoK</fr:link> for the corrected attributions.
</html:p>
